  "body": "## What changed\n\n1. **Auto reads the depth in material.** Auto chose the drill cycle by `R plane - bottom`, so the air above a hole's mouth counted as depth. A 3.5 mm spot under a 5 mm gap posted `G73 ... Q18`, with a peck step longer than the hole. Auto now reads the depth from the mouth (`Hole::entry_z`), or from the R plane when the R plane is lower. These readers use the new depth:\n   - the axial cycle (`crates/motion/src/drilling/cycle.rs`);\n   - the radial cycle (`cross.rs`, from d = 0, not from the R standoff);\n   - the setup sheet (`crates/app/src/setup_sheet/operations.rs`).\n\n   The drill page note already read `entry_z - floor_z`, so generation now agrees with the page. The plunge still starts at the R plane, and the R word does not change.\n2. **A new cycle choice `Deep`.** In the project file and MCP it is `\"deep\"`. In the combo it is \"Deep peck (full retract)\". It gives the existing `CycleKind::Deep`, which every canned-cycle post writes as `G83`. It is appended at combo index 10 and digest byte 10, so older operations keep their indices and stamps. The cross-hole cycle maps it before its `unreachable!` arm.\n3. **The cycle words are listed.** `list_operation_types` already lists them (#3449). The test now also asks for `deep`.\n\nDocs: the Drill section of `site/content/guide/operations/operations-2d.md`, and the decision file `docs/decisions/2443-drill-auto-depth.md`.\n\n**Effect on programs.** Under Auto, a hole whose R plane is high above its mouth can change from `G83` to `G73`, or from `G73` to `G81`. The catalog case `2d/first-part` changes its four holes from `G83 ... Q6` to `G73 ... Q18` (R plane Z22). Only that case's `.nc` is rebuilt. Its `.camproj` was already stale on main (version 71), and the catalog tests compare the program only. `cargo xtask catalog --check` passes on every case.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-motion` lib, `drilling::tests_auto_depth`:\n  - `auto_measures_a_spot_from_its_mouth_not_from_the_r_plane` (the issue's case: G81, not G73)\n  - `auto_reads_a_lower_r_plane_as_the_start_of_the_depth`\n  - `the_deep_choice_is_the_full_retract_cycle`\n  - `a_cross_hole_reads_its_depth_from_the_mouth_and_takes_deep`\n- `mcp` suite: `drill_deep::the_deep_cycle_word_posts_full_retract_pecks_and_rides_the_project_file` (Auto posts G73, `deep` posts G83 through Fanuc, and the word survives a save and an open). `op_type_fields::list_operation_types_names_the_optional_fields_and_enum_words` now asks for `deep`.\n- `camcraft-ui` lib: `cycle_combo::the_deep_peck_reads_in_plain_english` and `every_cycle_has_one_label_and_picks_itself_back` (11 choices).\n- `example_catalog`: `catalog_2d_first_part::{rebuilds,regenerates}` with the rebuilt program.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`, head 582d9dc80): 82 steps, 1 failed, `example_catalog` `catalog_2d_first_part`. The failure was the intended program change above. 46edb3521 rebuilds the case. `example_catalog` passes on the final head (44 tests).\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps --all-targets -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Site tests: no failure that main does not have.\n- Heavy lanes (`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`): running. I will add the result in a comment. The PR is not ready until then.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A real machine.\n\nChangelog: Drill: Auto chooses the cycle by the depth in material, measured from each hole's mouth, not from the R plane (a shallow spot under a high R plane now drills with G81). New cycle choice \"Deep peck (full retract)\" (`deep`) posts G83 on any hole.\n\nFixes #2443\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
